  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile achieves the best performance (0.650-0.653), while image-only models are near chance (~0.21-0.23), indicating image is a very weak signal. The critical open question is whether fusing this weak image modality with the strong RNA signal can improve upon the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. This experiment (config_031: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted fusion) directly tests that question using the best-known RNA encoder and profile setting. Weighted fusion is chosen over concat because it can learn to downweight the weak image features, making it the more robust fusion strategy when modality strengths are highly asymmetric. If this does not exceed ~0.653, we can confidently conclude image adds no value and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinement; if it does, we gain evidence that multimodal fusion is worthwhile and should explore further."
}

